WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.089 --> 00:00:08.591
Lisey’s Story is a story
of a woman’s courage.

00:00:13.221 --> 00:00:18.435
It’s about a woman who
is trying to find herself

00:00:18.435 --> 00:00:21.813
again after the loss
of her husband.

00:00:24.107 --> 00:00:27.652
It’s a relatable story of
family and marriage,

00:00:27.652 --> 00:00:31.197
and then it goes to a place
that only a wild imagination

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:32.991
like Stephen King’s could take you.

00:00:35.994 --> 00:00:39.247
It’s a very scary
story in a lot of ways.

00:00:39.247 --> 00:00:43.043
It’s scary in a supernatural way
but it’s also scary because 

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:45.378
there really are dangerous
people out there.

00:00:50.592 --> 00:00:52.927
This is a story about
love and relationships

00:00:52.927 --> 00:00:54.220
and how we save each other.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:01.311
It’s so multi-layered, you know.
It’s terribly romantic.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:04.189
It’s terrifying at times.

00:01:04.189 --> 00:01:08.068
And it’s upsetting and it’s
full of pain and beauty.

00:01:09.277 --> 00:01:11.362
Lisey is completely grief stricken.

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:14.491
I’ve left Lisey a bool hunt.

00:01:14.491 --> 00:01:19.454
I’ve given her clues that she
is diving into with her grief.

00:01:20.288 --> 00:01:22.290
Nobody really knows what
goes on in a marriage

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:23.666
except the two people who are in it.

00:01:26.294 --> 00:01:29.172
What is that world that only
the two of them know about?

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:33.593
Lisey is kind of drawn into this world.

00:01:37.806 --> 00:01:41.518
Lisey is trying to save her
sister and save her husband

00:01:41.518 --> 00:01:43.937
and then there’s this kind
of outside pressure where

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:45.897
someone is menacing her all the time.

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:52.529
When Scott dies, my character wants
his unpublished works to be published.

00:01:52.529 --> 00:01:56.908
He thinks Lisey is holding
them away from the public,

00:01:56.908 --> 00:01:59.994
so he makes it his mission
and he’ll do pretty much

00:01:59.994 --> 00:02:01.746
anything to make sure that happens.

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:05.542
Secrets secrets are no fun.
Secrets secrets hurt someone.

00:02:08.753 --> 00:02:11.464
We are straddling whole
different worlds and in

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:12.799
some ways whole different genres.

00:02:14.676 --> 00:02:17.053
I think that in and of
itself is really unusual,

00:02:19.389 --> 00:02:22.600
to have this kind of horror,
this supernatural element.

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:23.560
Where'd you go?

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:24.477
Come back.

00:02:28.022 --> 00:02:33.403
It’s very unique and unusual,
a really strong, beautiful vision.

00:02:34.112 --> 00:02:36.531
It just works on so many levels.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:41.995
Stephen King has crafted
this beautiful story.

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:45.582
He’s someone who’s
been able to understand

00:02:45.582 --> 00:02:48.668
our humanity in
a very universal way.

00:02:51.921 --> 00:02:53.715
This is a love story.

00:02:56.551 --> 00:02:58.720
It’s a beautiful, unearthly thing.

